This product is an independent, clean-room Rust implementation of the context
compression system described by the Headroom project:

    https://github.com/headroomlabs-ai/headroom
    Copyright the Headroom Maintainers, licensed under Apache License 2.0

"Clean-room" here is a statement about method, not a disclaimer. The
architecture, the cache-safety invariants, the compressor taxonomy, and the
public command and tool surface implemented here were derived from Headroom's
*published documentation* — its README, its REALIGNMENT design documents, and
its user-facing docs — rather than from its source code. The implementation in
this repository was written independently.

Headroom is gratefully acknowledged as the origin of the design. In particular,
the insight that context compression must treat the provider prompt cache as
sacred — compressing only the live zone while leaving the frozen prefix
byte-identical — is theirs, and it is the load-bearing idea this project is
built around.
